data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/summary.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign summary: greet, tested\\n\\n## Mission\\nDeliver `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` and\\n`tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string, with\\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exiting 0.\\n\\n## What happened\\n- Dispatched d002 to `dev` with the exact deliverables and scope (only\\n  `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py`).\\n- `dev` implemented `greet(name)` as `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"` and added\\n  `tests/test_greet.py` with `test_normal_name` and `test_empty_string`,\\n  committed as `533b244` (\\\"Add greet(name) function with unittest coverage\\\")\\n  on top of base `2e8ce27`.\\n- Judged by fetching `dev`'s branch (not just trusting the reply): checked\\n  out commit `533b244` in a clean checkout and independently ran\\n  `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` — exit code 0, both tests passed.\\n  Diff confirmed only the two named files were touched.\\n- Accepted d002 from `dev`.\\n\\n## Outcome\\nAll three stated criteria are satisfied:\\n1. `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` — done.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string — done.\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 — verified independently.\\n\\nReporting `campaign-met`.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

